XRLF.PROMPT.START

PROMPT.IDENTITY:
  Name := LLM_PROVIDER_CUSTOM_SKELETON
  Type := XLR_Skeleton_Prompt
  Source := .env:365-366 (LUMAX_LLM_PROVIDER=custom)
  Compressor := Tools/foveated-memory/core/xrl-compressor.js
  CompressionLevel := 3 (Deep ~88%)

PROMPT.SCOPE:
  This prompt skeleton defines the XLR-compressed representation of the
  LUMAX custom OpenAI-compatible LLM provider configuration. It captures
  the essential structure, request format, and integration points while
  stripping all redundant prose — matching the foveated memory ring
  compression philosophy from xrl-compressor.js.

PROMPT.CONTEXT:
  ▸ Custom OpenAI-compatible provider — LUMAX_LLM_PROVIDER=custom
  The LUMAX system routes LLM requests through a custom provider that
  speaks the OpenAI Chat Completions API format but targets a
  configurable backend (Ollama, LM Studio, or any compatible endpoint).

PROMPT.ENV_VARS (Skeleton):
  LUMAX_LLM_PROVIDER=custom
  LUMAX_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
  LUMAX_MODEL_ID=<model_hash>@q4_0
  LUMAX_API_KEY=<api_key>
  LUMAX_CLOUD_MODEL=kimi-2.7-code
  LUMAX_COMPRESSOR_MODEL=smart-router_gguf
  LUMAX_COMPRESSOR_MODEL_NO2=no.2-smart-router_gguf
  LUMAX_RECIEVER_MODEL=smart-router_gguf
  LUMAX_DELEGATOR_MODEL=no.2-smart-router_gguf
  LUMAX_CPU_ONLY_MODELS=smart-router_gguf,no.2-smart-router_gguf,reasoning-summarizer-800m-pre
  LUMAX_LLM_SUMMARIZE=true
  LUMAX_SUMMARIZER_MODEL=reasoning-summarizer-800m-pre
  LM_STUDIO_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7272

PROMPT.REQUEST_FORMAT (OpenAI-Compatible Skeleton):
  POST {LUMAX_BASE_URL}/chat/completions
  Headers:
    Authorization: Bearer {LUMAX_API_KEY}
    Content-Type: application/json
  Body:
    {
      "model": "{LUMAX_MODEL_ID}",
      "messages": [
        {"role": "system", "content": "<system_prompt>"},
        {"role": "user", "content": "<user_message>"}
      ],
      "stream": true,
      "temperature": 0.7
    }

PROMPT.XRL_COMPRESSION_MAP:
  The XRL compressor (xrl-compressor.js) applies 6 foveated ring levels:
    Level 0 — Raw (0%): Verbatim messages, tone-classified refinement
    Level 1 — Light (~50%): Extractive top-scoring sentences + headline
    Level 2 — Medium (~75%): Key sentences + topic + headline
    Level 3 — Deep (~88%): Headline + topic + first meaningful sentence
    Level 4 — Ultra (~95%): Headline + topic label + xrl:// hash ref
    Level 5 — Atomic (~98%): Headline + xrl:// hash only

  For the custom provider, conversation history is compressed before
  being sent to the LLM endpoint. The compressor selects the ring level
  based on message age and token budget.

PROMPT.ROUTING_LOGIC (Skeleton):
  IF LUMAX_LLM_PROVIDER == "custom":
    endpoint := LUMAX_BASE_URL + "/chat/completions"
    model := LUMAX_MODEL_ID
    auth := "Bearer " + LUMAX_API_KEY
    format := OpenAI_Chat_Completions
    streaming := true
    fallback := LUMAX_CLOUD_MODEL (kimi-2.7-code)

PROMPT.RELATED_FILES:
  - .env (lines 340-366) — Provider configuration
  - Tools/foveated-memory/core/xrl-compressor.js — Ring compression engine
  - .xrlf/prompts/llm-provider-custom.schema.json — Machine-readable schema
  - .xrlf/prompts/llm-provider-custom.example.js — Usage example

